  <text>
    <body>
      <div>
        <head>In the directories</head>
        <p>John Hudspeth, painter, is listed in <ref target="civic?id=Leicester%20Street">Leicester Street</ref> from 1864 to 1890. He is at No. 73 for most of that time (No. 75 from 1866 to 1868), and at No. 137 in 1890, after the street was renumbered. In 1862 a Hudspeth with no first name or trade is listed at No. 73, and that listing is linked here too.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <head>Neighbours</head>
        <p>William Cecil, general dealer and later grocer, is at No. 65 in 1862 and 1867, and Betsy Irving, grocer, at No. 75 from 1867 to 1869. From 1870 to 1890 his next-door neighbour is Laurence Angus, grocer, at No. 75 and then No. 139. W. Lawrence, general carrier, is on the other side at No. 71 in 1872.</p>
      </div>
